  "headline": "Granisetron hydrochloride is not on FDA's shortage list; supply traces to a plant with multiple VAI inspections",
  "headline_cites": ["D3", "E7"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA's drug shortage list does not include granisetron hydrochloride as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["D3"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The product label for NDC 69452035001 identifies OrBion Pharmaceuticals Private Limited (FEI 3004540907) as the manufacturing plant.",
      "cites": ["E7"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection records show that plant received VAI classifications on 2011-04-07, 2015-06-03, 2019-05-31, and 2023-09-08.",
      "cites": ["E3", "E4", "E5", "E6"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The most recent inspection ended 2023-09-08 with a VAI classification known to FDA on 2023-10-11.",
      "cites": ["E6"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The label's last inspection entry for that plant is NAI dated 2025-10-27.",
      "cites": ["E7"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East holds 204 tablets of the 1 mg presentation at 7.6 tablets per day (26.8 days on hand) and Corvale General holds 135 tablets at 9.1 per day (14.9 days on hand).",
      "cites": ["D1", "D2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule-based best option is to buy from Breckenridge Pharmaceutical, Inc., which is not on FDA's shortage list today, though its label names no plant we could place.",
      "cites": ["D4"]
    }
  ]
}
